From 8b2eee06569031bd9d7caac29344ed77eea392bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anthony Ruhier <aruhier@mailbox.org>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 13:27:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] NVMe dynamic BW scale

https://github.com/qualcomm-linux/kernel/pull/1238

FROMLIST: nvme: Add adaptive PCIe link rate switching function
FROMLIST: nvme: Add hysteresis and idle detection to link rate switching
FROMLIST: nvme: Expose link rate switching tunables via sysfs
FROMLIST: PCI: qcom: Enable Link Bandwidth Notification capability

The PR's "PCI/bwctrl: Set host bridge OPP..." and "PCI: qcom: Enable ASPM
disabling during link retraining" are already in the bwscale series
above, as is the pcie_set_target_speed() export from the first patch.
Instead of the PR's qcom.config change, enable CONFIG_NVME_SPEED_SWITCH
in aruhier.config.

Signed-off-by: Liao Xuan <liaoxuan@open-hieco.net>
Signed-off-by: Krishna Chaitanya Chundru <krishna.chundru@oss.qualcomm.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
